## 7. Frequently asked questions

| Question | Answer |
|----------|--------|
| **Do I need Internet permission?** | Only if you also load HTTP/HTTPS tiles. For pure `vault://` tiles you can omit `<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET"/>`. |
| **Can I cache the decrypted tiles?** | Yes. The handler can write the decrypted bytes to a local cache directory (e.g. `context.cacheDir`) and return the cached file on subsequent requests. |
| **What about vector-tile-specific headers?** | The SDK does not require any special headers for MVT. Supplying `Content-Type: application/vnd.mapbox-vector-tile` is optional but nice for debugging. |
| **Will this work with raster sources (e.g. `raster` or `raster-dem`)?** | Absolutely – the same handler is used for *any* URL. Just return the appropriate image bytes (PNG/JPEG) for raster sources. |
| **Is there a way to register a handler only for a specific source?** | No, the handler is global. Inside `handleRequest` you can inspect the URL (or query parameters) and decide to process only the ones you care about. |
| **Can I use `HttpRequestHandlerFactory` instead?** | Yes. If you need different handlers for different schemes you can implement `HttpRequestHandlerFactory` and return a handler per request. The SDK will call `factory.create(request)` for each request. |
| **What about MapLibre 11+ where the SDK moved to `org.maplibre.gl`?** | The API is unchanged – the class names are still `MapLibre`, `MapLibreOptions`, `HttpRequestHandler`. Just import from the new package. |

